---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/ipsas/accrual-ipsas-jan2025.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  covers={metadata.covers}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Purpose & Structure of This Appendix" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Table A — Standards Effective as at January 1, 2025 (Summary)" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Table B — Standards Not Yet Effective as at January 1, 2025" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Table C — Standards No Longer Effective as at January 1, 2025" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Reading the Full Table A's Amendment-Tracking Columns" },
        { id: "s6", label: "This Library's Coverage — a Complete Set" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <LifecycleNotice
    type="active"
    explanation="Summary of Accrual IPSAS Standards Issued as of January 2025 brings together all accrual-basis IPSAS on issue as of January 31, 2025 from Volume III of the 2025 IPSASB Handbook, summarizing Table A (effective standards), Table B (issued but not yet effective), and Table C (withdrawn)."
    link=""
    linkText=""
  />

  <!-- ============ SECTION 1 — PURPOSE & STRUCTURE OF THIS APPENDIX ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Purpose &amp; Structure of This Appendix</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">A Handbook appendix, not a Standard — the master index of everything else in this library</div>
      <div class="principle">This appendix (Handbook pages 702–733) closes out Volume III of the 2025 IPSASB Handbook, immediately following the Glossary of Defined Terms. It brings together, in one place, EVERY accrual-basis IPSAS on issue as of January 31, 2025 — cross-referenced against every Standard poster built throughout this library (IPSAS 1–51).</div>
      <div class="dot-list">
        <span><strong>Table A</strong> — Standards EFFECTIVE as at January 1, 2025, with paragraph-level tracking of any provisions not yet effective</span>
        <span><strong>Table B</strong> — Standards issued but NOT YET effective as at that date</span>
        <span><strong>Table C</strong> — Standards NO LONGER effective, having been superseded and withdrawn</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note">The full Table A runs to paragraph-level amendment tracking across ~28 Handbook pages — genuinely exhaustive detail already captured, Standard by Standard, in each individual poster's own "Effective Date &amp; Amendment Timeline" section throughout this library. This poster condenses Table A into a clean summary (issue date + original effective date per Standard), while reproducing Tables B and C in full, since both are compact and genuinely useful at a glance.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 2 — TABLE A: CURRENTLY EFFECTIVE STANDARDS ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Table A — Standards Effective as at January 1, 2025 (Summary)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">All 43 currently-effective accrual IPSAS, issue and original effective dates</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>IPSAS Standard</span><span>Issued</span><span>Original Effective Date</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>1, Presentation of Financial Statements</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>2, Cash Flow Statements</span><span>May 2000</span><span>Jul 1, 2001</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>3, Accounting Policies, Estimates and Errors</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>4, Effects of Changes in Foreign Exchange Rates</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>5, Borrowing Costs</span><span>May 2000</span><span>Jul 1, 2001</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>9, Revenue from Exchange Transactions</span><span>Jul 2001</span><span>Jul 1, 2002</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>10, Hyperinflationary Economies</span><span>Jul 2001</span><span>Jul 1, 2002</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>11, Construction Contracts</span><span>Jul 2001</span><span>Jul 1, 2002</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>12, Inventories</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>14, Events after the Reporting Date</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>16, Investment Property</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>18, Segment Reporting</span><span>Jun 2002</span><span>Jul 1, 2003</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>19, Provisions, Contingent Liabilities and Assets</span><span>Oct 2002</span><span>Jul 1, 2003</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>20, Related Party Disclosures</span><span>Oct 2002</span><span>Jul 1, 2003</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>21, Impairment of Non-Cash-Generating Assets</span><span>Dec 2004</span><span>Jan 1, 2006</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>22, Disclosure of Financial Information about the GGS</span><span>Dec 2006</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>23, Revenue from Non-Exchange Transactions</span><span>Dec 2006</span><span>Jan 1, 2008</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>24, Presentation of Budget Information</span><span>Dec 2006</span><span>Jan 1, 2009</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>26, Impairment of Cash-Generating Assets</span><span>Feb 2008</span><span>Jan 1, 2009</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>27, Agriculture</span><span>Dec 2009</span><span>Apr 1, 2011</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>28, Financial Instruments: Presentation</span><span>Jan 2010</span><span>Jan 1, 2013</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>29, Financial Instruments: Recognition and Measurement</span><span>Jan 2010</span><span>Jan 1, 2013</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>30, Financial Instruments: Disclosures</span><span>Jan 2010</span><span>Jan 1, 2013</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>31, Intangible Assets</span><span>Jan 2010</span><span>Apr 1, 2011</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>32, Service Concession Arrangements: Grantor</span><span>Oct 2011</span><span>Jan 1, 2014</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>33, First-time Adoption of Accrual Basis IPSAS</span><span>Jan 2015</span><span>Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>34, Separate Financial Statements</span><span>Jan 2015</span><span>Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>35, Consolidated Financial Statements</span><span>Jan 2015</span><span>Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>36, Investments in Associates and Joint Ventures</span><span>Jan 2015</span><span>Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>37, Joint Arrangements</span><span>Jan 2015</span><span>Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>38, Disclosure of Interests in Other Entities</span><span>Jan 2015</span><span>Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>39, Employee Benefits</span><span>Jul 2016</span><span>Jan 1, 2018</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>40, Public Sector Combinations</span><span>Jan 2017</span><span>Jan 1, 2019</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>41, Financial Instruments</span><span>Aug 2018</span><span>Jan 1, 2023</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>42, Social Benefits</span><span>Jan 2019</span><span>Jan 1, 2023</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>43, Leases</span><span>Jan 2022</span><span>Jan 1, 2025</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>44, Non-current Assets Held for Sale and Discontinued Operations</span><span>May 2022</span><span>Jan 1, 2025</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>45, Property, Plant, and Equipment</span><span>May 2023</span><span>Jan 1, 2025</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>46, Measurement</span><span>May 2023</span><span>Jan 1, 2025</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">Excludes withdrawn Standards 6, 7, 8, 13, 15, 17, 25 (Table C, &sect;4) and not-yet-effective Standards 47–51 (Table B, &sect;3).</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 3 — TABLE B: STANDARDS NOT YET EFFECTIVE ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Table B — Standards Not Yet Effective as at January 1, 2025</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">The four newest Standards, each with a coordinated consequential-amendment footprint</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 0.8fr 0.9fr 1.7fr;"><span>IPSAS Standard</span><span>Issued</span><span>Effective</span><span>Other IPSAS Affected</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 0.8fr 0.9fr 1.7fr;"><span>47, Revenue</span><span>May 2023</span><span>Jan 1, 2026</span><span>1, 2, 4, 5, 9, 12, 16, 17, 18, 19, 21, 24, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 35, 40, 41, 43, 44, 45</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 0.8fr 0.9fr 1.7fr;"><span>48, Transfer Expenses</span><span>May 2023</span><span>Jan 1, 2026</span><span>4, 12, 33, 40, 42</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 0.8fr 0.9fr 1.7fr;"><span>49, Retirement Benefit Plans</span><span>Nov 2023</span><span>Jan 1, 2026</span><span>39, 41</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 0.8fr 0.9fr 1.7fr;"><span>50, Exploration for and Evaluation of Mineral Resources</span><span>Nov 2024</span><span>Jan 1, 2027</span><span>31, 33, 45</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">IPSAS 47's affected-Standards list is by far the LONGEST in the Handbook — reflecting how deeply "revenue" touches nearly every other area of accrual accounting. All of these Standards have full extended posters built in this library.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 4 — TABLE C: STANDARDS NO LONGER EFFECTIVE ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Table C — Standards No Longer Effective as at January 1, 2025</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">Seven superseded Standards — each covered as a redirect-stub poster in this library</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>IPSAS Standard</span><span>Issued</span><span>Reason &amp; Date No Longer Effective</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>6, Consolidated and Separate Financial Statements</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Superseded by IPSAS 34–35, periods from Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>7, Investments in Associates</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Superseded by IPSAS 36, periods from Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>8, Interests in Joint Ventures</span><span>Dec 2006 (rev.)</span><span>Superseded by IPSAS 37, periods from Jan 1, 2017</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>13, Leases</span><span>Dec 2001</span><span>Superseded by IPSAS 43, periods from Jan 1, 2025</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>15, Financial Instruments: Disclosure and Presentation</span><span>Dec 2001</span><span>Superseded by IPSAS 28–30, periods from Jan 1, 2013</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>17, Property, Plant, and Equipment</span><span>Dec 2001</span><span>Superseded by IPSAS 45, periods from Jan 1, 2025</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr 2fr;"><span>25, Employee Benefits</span><span>Feb 2008</span><span>Superseded by IPSAS 39, periods from Jan 1, 2018</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 5 — READING THE AMENDMENT-TRACKING COLUMNS ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Reading the Full Table A's Amendment-Tracking Columns</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">What the six-column format in the Handbook's own Table A shows</div>
      <div class="text-supporting" style="margin-bottom:8px;">The Handbook's full Table A (pages 702–729) tracks, for EVERY IPSAS with paragraphs not yet effective, six pieces of information per paragraph: the STANDARD, its paragraph NUMBER, whether that paragraph is NEW or AMENDED, the ORIGIN of the amendment (which later Standard or Improvements project introduced it), the origin's OWN effective date, and the HANDBOOK EDITION containing the paragraph's original text.</div>
      <div class="dot-list">
        <span>Example: IPSAS 1 para. 50 — AMENDED by IPSAS 47 (2022) — shows that IPSAS 47's issuance, though not yet effective until 2026 (&sect;3), already introduced a consequential amendment to IPSAS 1's text, itself not yet effective</span>
        <span>Example: IPSAS 1 paras. 70, 80, 82, 84, 85, 87 — AMENDED by Improvements to IPSAS, 2023, all originally appearing in the 2024 Handbook edition</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note">This granular tracking is exactly what each individual Standard's own "Effective Date &amp; Amendment Timeline" section in this library already documents, Standard by Standard — see any individual poster for its own paragraph-level detail.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 6 — THIS LIBRARY'S COVERAGE ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>This Library's Coverage — a Complete Set</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2">
      <div class="ctitle cs">Every Standard in this appendix has its own extended poster</div>
      <div class="dot-list">
        <span><strong>Preface to IPSAS</strong> and the <strong>Conceptual Framework</strong> — the front-matter foundation</span>
        <span><strong>IPSAS 1–46</strong> — all 43 currently-effective Standards (Table A above), each as a full extended poster</span>
        <span><strong>IPSAS 6, 7, 8, 13, 15, 17, 25</strong> — withdrawn Standards (Table C above), each as a redirect-stub poster</span>
        <span><strong>IPSAS 47–51</strong> — newly issued and future standards, each fully covered</span>
        <span><strong>Cash Basis IPSAS</strong> (Introduction + full Standard, Parts 1 &amp; 2) — the parallel cash-basis track</span>
        <span><strong>Introduction to RPGs</strong>, and <strong>RPG 1, 2, 3</strong> — the non-authoritative good-practice guideline series</span>
        <span><strong>IPSASB SRS 1</strong> — the inaugural sustainability reporting standard</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
